# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and on checkout on every
# platform. Without this, a Windows checkout converts LF to CRLF and
# `cargo fmt --check` fails against rustfmt.toml's `newline_style = "Unix"`.
# Pinning the ending here keeps Windows and Linux byte-identical, which is what the
# Windows-first strategy in ADR-0002 requires.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# The npm lock is an independently audited, SHA-256-pinned artifact. Preserve its exact
# bytes across platforms so checkout cannot invalidate the approved digest.
web/package-lock.json -text
